## 1. The experiments, oldest first

Each entry gives: the question; the design; the pre-registered result line as read; the key numbers; the status; and where the record lives.

### E1. stance4 round: stagger penalty (2026-10-19 to 2026-10-20)

- **Question.** Does a left-right stagger penalty (weight 0.30, tolerance 0.045 m) on the L+T stance recipe fix the fore-aft foot fault (tests K1-K4)? [measured, RUNLOG l.2-4] The tail was not the question [inferred, RUNLOG l.1-7 name no tail aim].
- **Design.** 3 runs, seeds 52, 60, 42, from scratch, 12M steps, Colab L4 GPU. Control: stance3 Runs 2 and 3, not retrained [measured, RUNLOG l.1-3, l.15-17].
- **Result line.** "DECISION (final, not provisional): line 5. Not adopted; next round tests the per-foot CoP band or the v6b ankle spring." [measured, RUNLOG l.172]
- **Key numbers.**
  - 0 of 3 runs hold. s42 fails K1-K4 [measured, RUNLOG l.170].
  - s42 saturation alarm (report only): at least 5 of 10 evaluation episodes flagged at every evaluation from 2,097,152 to 3,538,944, and 10 of 10 at 3,670,016. s52 and s60: none [measured, RUNLOG l.93-95].
  - s42 judged 0 of 40 clean at 4.19M and 6.29M, and 14 of 40 at the final [measured, RUNLOG l.108-109, l.136, l.163].
  - Two side studies were about the foot, not the tail: stagger replicate continuations (line 2, partial) and a CoP-band continuation test (line 2, partial) [measured, RUNLOG l.101-107, l.144-148].
- **Status.** Final [measured, RUNLOG l.172].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.1-207. Run branch `screen-trex-r9-armlt-stagger` at c1e146a8 [measured, RUNLOG l.21]. Records PR #633, merged 2026-10-20 22:11 UTC [measured, RUNLOG l.208, l.216].

### E2. Saturation diagnosis of stance4 s42 (2026-10-20 to 2026-10-21)

- **Question.** Which actuator saturates in s42, and is it the command, the joint or the motor? [measured, RUNLOG l.199-201]
- **Design.** Offline rollouts of s42's checkpoints, report only (maintainer decision 5a: no training change; tell the maintainer at once when an alarm fires) [measured, RUNLOG l.197-201].
- **Result (no pre-registered line).** "tail_3_pitch_act commanded at +1 (tail tip up; command pinned, joint and motor not: joint 0.216 rad below its stop on 0.26 of its force), same actuator and sign as stance3 Run 2" [measured, RUNLOG l.227-228].
- **Key numbers.**
  - Onset between 1.05M and 2.10M; ledger flags from 1,835,008 [measured, RUNLOG l.228-229].
  - Holding tail_3 at 0 gains +85.9 (at 2.1M) and +73.1 (at the final) reward per 800-step window, deterministic. "Why training keeps it is not measured." [measured, RUNLOG l.229-230]
  - The ledger then had no per-actuator column, so it could not name the actuator [measured, RUNLOG l.230].
- **Status.** Final, report only. Candidate fixes listed; none acted on [measured, RUNLOG l.230-231].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.199-231. TAILREC row L035 (line 603). Its run-log lines are in the copy carried by #634 [measured, RUNLOG l.412].

### E3. stance5 round: per-foot CoP band (2026-10-21 to 2026-10-22)

- **Question.** Does a per-foot CoP band on top of stance4's recipe (arm LTSB) fix the foot fault? [measured, RUNLOG l.181-187]
- **Design.** 3 runs, seeds 52, 60, 42, from scratch, 12M steps, Colab L4. Control: stance4's three runs [measured, RUNLOG l.185-187, l.239-245].
- **Result line.** "DECISION (final, not provisional): line 3. "H == 1: not adopted; not separated from seed luck; replicate on 2 more seeds before any commit."" [measured, RUNLOG l.351-352]
- **Key numbers.**
  - s52 holds; s60 fails K3 only; s42 fails K1 and K3 [measured, RUNLOG l.349].
  - s42 tail alarm at 3,670,016 (first flagged evaluation 3,538,944). Named: tail_3_pitch_act at +1, |command| at least 0.9 on 77% of window steps at 4,194,304 [measured, RUNLOG l.262-266].
  - s42's final: 19 of 40 clean, 20 saturation-rail episodes [measured, RUNLOG l.335, l.366].
  - s52 and s60: no saturation flag in 52 evaluations each, up to 6,815,744 [measured, RUNLOG l.303].
- **Status.** Final [measured, RUNLOG l.351].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.181-369. Run branch `screen-trex-r9-armlts-copband` at cf80ecb1 [measured, RUNLOG l.236]. Records PR #634, merged 2026-10-22 19:41 UTC [measured, RUNLOG l.411, l.427].

### E4. Scratch tail experiment P1, and the K3 diagnosis (2026-10-22)

- **Question.** (a) Can a training-loss penalty on the policy's mean beyond ±1 ("P1") keep tail_3 off the rail? (b) Are stance5 s42's joint-noise falls (test K3) the tail habit? [measured, RUNLOG l.378-380]
- **Design.** P1: coefficient 41 on |mean| > 1. One seed. Two 1M-step CPU continuations (P1 and a control) from stance5 s42 at 4,194,304. Scratch clone, never pushed [measured, RUNLOG l.378-381, l.438-439].
- **Result (no pre-registered line).**
  - P1: tail_3's saturated share was lower than the paired control at 8 of 8 checkpoints (means 0.26 against 0.86). It reached 0.000 twice, then relapsed to 0.47 and 0.49 [measured, RUNLOG l.438].
  - It did NOT keep the deterministic mean within +1 (beyond +1 on 21-46% of window steps at 7 of 9 checkpoints). It only cut training rows beyond +1 (2.5% against 27.5%) [measured, RUNLOG l.438].
  - The original run without P1 read 0.171 at 5,242,880, below P1's 0.470. "The effect against training alone is not established." [measured, RUNLOG l.438]
  - K3: s42's falls are NOT the tail habit. Holding tail_3 at 0 leaves 9/9, 5/5, 9/9 and 12/13 of them. Hip-pitch noise is the main cause [measured, RUNLOG l.435].
- **Status.** Final, report only. P1 not adopted [measured, RUNLOG l.438; TAILREC line 1314].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.378-381, l.433-439. S1 `stance5/tailexp/report.md` and `stance5/k3diag/report.md` [measured, RUNLOG l.434]. TAILREC rows L049, L051.

### E5. stance5 replication: seeds 70 and 80 (2026-10-22 to 2026-10-24)

- **Question.** Does the unchanged band recipe hold on two new seeds? Adopt only if both hold [measured, RUNLOG l.370-374].
- **Design.** 2 runs, seeds 70 and 80, from scratch, 12M steps, Colab L4, branch at cf80ecb1 [measured, RUNLOG l.370-377, l.396-399].
