### E7. Tail options study and no-training probes (2026-10-24)

- **Question.** What holds the tail on the rail: the plant, the reward, the action clip, or the policy's own feedback? And what should the tail round test? [measured, RUNLOG l.504, l.509]
- **Design.** No training. CPU probes on r9 model copies and on the 4,194,304 checkpoints of stance5 s42 and stance5r s80. Two skeptic reviews [measured, RUNLOG l.504, l.508, l.517, l.525].
- **Result (no pre-registered line).**
  - The plant does not force the pin. A level distal tail would need a command of +1.073, which is out of range [measured, RUNLOG l.508].
  - No reward term pays for tail-up [measured, RUNLOG l.508]. Holding tail_3 at 0 gains reward in 40 of 40 paired noisy episodes: s42 +54.6 (95% CI +51.5 to +57.5), s80 +36.2 (+31.8 to +40.5) per window [measured, RUNLOG l.526].
  - Without the clip, the mean settles at a stable fixed point of a positive feedback loop (in-episode slope about 0.5-0.6); fixed points 0.45-1.07 across s42 episodes [measured, RUNLOG l.527].
  - The `policy_probe.npz` bank is not an early detector [measured, RUNLOG l.528].
  - The skeptics rejected a 5-seed from-scratch round of a 0.90 bound: 5 seeds cannot separate from chance (0 of 8 against 2 of 5 still gives p 0.13) [measured, RUNLOG l.508].
- **Status.** Final (analysis) [measured, RUNLOG l.518, l.525].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.504-528. S2 `tailround/` (`brief_v2.md`, `probes/`). TAILREC rows L061-L073.

### E8. tail_3 bound screen, D-D43 (2026-10-24 to 2026-10-25)

- **Question.** Does a training-loss bound on tail_3's mean (upper side only) bring the tail off the rail without parking it? [measured, RUNLOG l.509, l.538]
- **Design.** 18 CPU continuations of 1M steps (4,194,304 to 5,242,880), on r9. Starts: stance5 s42 and stance5r s80 at 4,194,304. Arms: CONTROL, BOUND90 (b = 0.90) and BOUND60 (b = 0.60), coefficient 2.4. 3 replicates (seeds 101, 202, 303) per arm per start. Approved 2026-10-24 19:06 UTC [measured, RUNLOG l.538, l.547-548, l.565-572].
- **Result line.** "OUTCOME C, no bound adopted." [measured, RUNLOG l.573]
- **Key numbers.**
  - BOUND90 NOT ADOPTED: RAIL in 6 of 6 (command 0.886-0.971) [measured, RUNLOG l.573].
  - BOUND60 NOT ADOPTED: PARKED in 6 of 6 with 0 tail-up flags (command 0.600-0.632) [measured, RUNLOG l.573].
  - CONTROL: s42 RAIL, CURED (seed 202, command 0.265), RAIL; s80 RAIL in 3 of 3 [measured, RUNLOG l.573].
  - Independent re-score: the score stands; 0 blocking findings [measured, RUNLOG l.575].
  - Under BOUND60, 52-59% of training rows still sat above b: "the outward drive persists" [measured, RUNLOG l.581].
- **Status.** Final, verified [measured, RUNLOG l.573, l.575].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.537-581. Durable `handoff-tailscreen` at 1106cd3 [measured, RUNLOG l.574]. Records PR #641, merged 2026-10-25 03:37 UTC [measured, RUNLOG l.578, l.591].

### E9. Posture options study (2026-10-25)

- **Question.** What did BOUND60 buy, and can r9 hold a better tail posture at all? [measured, RUNLOG l.576, l.579]
- **Design.** No training; screen traces, anatomy, costs; two skeptics [measured, RUNLOG l.579].
- **Result.** BOUND60's tail sat 1.2° lower than the walking-pilot parent. Every arm's distal tail sat 22-28° below horizontal, tail_1 on its ventral (lower) stop [measured, RUNLOG l.581]. This led to a plant probe (E10).
- **Status.** Final (analysis) [measured, RUNLOG l.581].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.579-582. S2 `tailround/posture/brief_corrected_summary.md` [measured, RUNLOG l.581].

### E10. r10 tail probe, CPU checks, and physics r10 (2026-10-25)

- **Question.** Can tail springs (a plant change) hold a level tail so that a level tail costs no command? [measured, RUNLOG l.582]
- **Design.** CPU only, scratch model copies, no training. Candidate SR3: spring rest angles 52.5° / 25.9° / 10.4° on the three tail pitch joints. Zero-shot closed loop of 8 r9 checkpoints; gate panels; the heading-test diagnosis [measured, RUNLOG l.583, l.585, l.589].
- **Result (no pre-registered line).**
  - SR3's statue rests with the tail straight; a level tail needs a command of about 0 (r9: 3.50 / 2.16 / 1.15) [measured, RUNLOG l.585].
  - Zero-shot, there is no sign SR3 cures the rail: saturation-failure episodes went 27 to 80. Old policies' tail inputs sit 5-8 SD outside their normaliser, so zero-shot cannot predict trained behaviour [measured, RUNLOG l.593].
  - r10 = SR3 was built and merged, with `tail_home_pose` re-centred (D-D44) [measured, RUNLOG l.597, l.606].
- **Status.** Done. r10 is the plant of record [measured, RUNLOG l.606]. It did NOT prevent the rail (E12) [measured, RUNLOG l.711].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.582-606. PRs #642 (heading test) and #643 (physics r10), merged 2026-10-25 14:08 UTC [measured, RUNLOG l.606].

