### E12. stance6: the first r10 round (2026-10-25 to 2026-10-28)

- **Question.** On physics r10, with the LTSB recipe, does the tail rail still form in training? Statistic A compares alarm runs with LTSB r9's 2 of 5 [measured, RUNLOG l.607, l.621].
- **Design.** 3 runs, seeds 60, 42, 80, from scratch, 12M steps (final 12,001,280), Colab L4. Branch `screen-trex-r10-armltsb` at 8737cd3d. Lean all-or-nothing criteria approved 2026-10-27 05:55 UTC [measured, RUNLOG l.610, l.614, l.621, l.664]. Launched about 14:57 UTC 2026-10-27; ends noted 06:25 UTC 2026-10-28 [measured, RUNLOG l.666, l.693-699].
- **Result line.** "READING line 1: TAIL RAIL FORMED ON r10 IN TRAINING (ledger); R 1 (COMPLETE 1, PRESENCE 0), U 0, P 1, G+ 1." STATUS FINAL [measured, RUNLOG l.711].
- **Key numbers.**
  - s42: RAIL, tail_3 at +1, first tail alarm 3,932,160, 22 alarms; gate certificate FAIL (hop_or_fall 2 > 1 at all six headings) [measured, RUNLOG l.711].
  - s60: PARKED, tail_3 MEAN_a +0.642 [measured, RUNLOG l.711].
  - s80: CLEAR on the tail, but 6 alarms on `neck_pitch_act`; gate PASS; POSITIVE [measured, RUNLOG l.711].
  - Statistic A: 2 of 3 against 2 of 5, one-sided Fisher p 0.93. Nothing significant. "An existence result, not a rate" [measured, S6HEAD lines 1-2].
  - Two report-only interim looks: none flagged at 3.01M; at 7.6M s42 alarming, s80 neck alarms, s60's tail_3 rising to +0.76 [measured, RUNLOG l.681, l.689].
  - Review on entropy: "no direct path to the mean" [inferred, S6HEAD line 6]. Next step proposed: ECS [measured, RUNLOG l.717].
- **Status.** Final [measured, RUNLOG l.711].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.607-728. Durable `handoff-stance6` (commits 6c3f27b9 and e4733d8) [measured, RUNLOG l.712, l.717]. Records PRs #647 (pre-registration, merged 2026-10-27 22:51 UTC) and #652 (results, merged 2026-10-29 00:28 UTC) [measured, RUNLOG l.687, l.728].

### E13. ECS: the entropy continuation screen (2026-10-28 to 2026-10-29)

- **Question.** From mid-rise states, does the remaining entropy bonus drive the crossing onto the rail? [measured, RUNLOG l.719-721]
- **Design.** 24 CPU continuations of 1,572,864 steps. Starts: stance6 s42 at 3,145,728 and s80 at 4,194,304. Arm A: entropy coefficient as recorded. Arm B: entropy coefficient 0. 6 per arm per start. Outcome-blind [measured, RUNLOG l.721; ECS `criteria.txt` lines 37-54].
- **Result line.** "line 3, NO DIFFERENCE DETECTED IN WHETHER AN ANY-FLAGGED EVALUATION CAME BY E FROM THESE STATES (not tested: a shift of the first flag within the window, a modest effect, the early phase)" [measured, RUNLOG l.740, l.742].
- **Key numbers.** s42: arm A 6 of 6, arm B 6 of 6. s80: arm A 1 of 6, arm B 1 of 6. P = 17/22 (0.77) both ways. s80's two positives are neck flags, not tail. All 24 counted; two independent checks agree [measured, RUNLOG l.740-741].
- **Status.** Final, verified [measured, RUNLOG l.740-741]. Entropy is not the driver from these states [inferred, from the line-3 reading; RUNLOG l.742 lists what it did not test].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.719-744. Durable `handoff-ecs` at 067b8a10 [measured, RUNLOG l.744]. Records PR #654 [measured, RUNLOG l.766, l.790].

### E14. CoM revisit, static CoM check and tail clamp test (2026-10-29)

- **Question.** Is the raised tail a counterweight? What happens if the rail is removed from railed policies, or imposed on unrailed ones? [measured, RUNLOG l.746-748]
- **Design.** Simulation only. A static check on the r10 model. Then 12 s42 ECS end policies with tail_3 held at 0, and 12 s80 end policies with tail_3 forced to +1; seeds 3042-3061 [measured, RUNLOG l.746-748].
- **Result (no pre-registered line; verified).**
  - tail_3 at its limits moves the whole-body centre of mass by +0.19 / +0.24 mm fore-aft and ±2.03 mm vertically: not a static counterweight [measured, RUNLOG l.746].
  - s42 held at 0: return +63.6 in 12 of 12; stance otherwise unchanged; head 3.5° lower [measured, RUNLOG l.750].
  - s80 forced to +1: return -180 in 12 of 12 [measured, RUNLOG l.750].
  - A positive feedback from the observed tail angle to the tail_3 command: loop gain about 0.63 in the s42 ends (0.27 at the start), fixed point past the +1 limit [measured, RUNLOG l.750].
- **Status.** Final, report only [measured, RUNLOG l.750].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.745-750. S2 `com_revisit/REPORT.txt` [measured, RUNLOG l.750]. Records PR #654.

### E15. Normaliser probe and posture tests (2026-10-29)

- **Question.** Does drift in the observation normaliser build the loop? Does a body posture drive the tail? [measured, RUNLOG l.751, l.754]
- **Design.** No training; ECS checkpoints and the r9/r10 records; one verifier [measured, RUNLOG l.751-754].
- **Result (verified with corrections).**
  - Normaliser drift opposes the gain growth; the network weights carry it [measured, RUNLOG l.757].
  - In r10 s42 a posture-independent tail bias rose first (about 1.20M); nose-down posture came about 0.17M later [measured, RUNLOG l.757].
  - The s42 networks map perceived nose-down pitch to a tail offset (-0.157 command per degree nose-up). Perceived +1.1° nose-up cut railed episodes from 0.67 to 0.15. This pathway was absent before the rise. s60 has the opposite pitch sensitivity [measured, RUNLOG l.757].
- **Status.** Final, report only [measured, RUNLOG l.757].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.751-758. TAILREC sections 4.8 and 4.11. Records PR #654 (merged 2026-10-30 13:36 UTC) [measured, RUNLOG l.790].

### E16. Early-bias probe (2026-10-30)

- **Question.** Which part of the training loss first pushes tail_3's mean up? [measured, RUNLOG l.763]
- **Design.** At stance6 checkpoints, rebuild one PPO update and measure each loss term's push on tail_3's mean. No optimizer step. A verifier fetched the 1,310,720 checkpoints [measured, RUNLOG l.763, l.771].
- **Result (verified with corrections).**
  - Only the policy-gradient term moves the mean. Entropy and value terms: exactly 0. Mirror-KL: small [measured, RUNLOG l.770-771].
  - At 1.31M, just after s42's onset (1.204M), s42 already has an upward pull carried by tail_3's own exploration noise: +0.00115 ± 0.00032 per epoch (t 3.6). s80 has none until about 0.8M later [measured, RUNLOG l.771].
  - The critic's bootstrap is a source from 2.10M on (GAE minus Monte Carlo +0.0037, t 3.7; +0.024, t 7.9 at 3.15M). At the onset it is unresolved (+0.0005 ± 0.00045) [measured, RUNLOG l.771].
  - The critic's slope on the tail angle is positive where the pull appears [measured, RUNLOG l.770-771]. The "tail angle as a clock" reading was then only a hypothesis [inferred, RUNLOG l.770-771].
- **Status.** Final [measured, RUNLOG l.771].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.763, l.770-771. Records PR #656.

### E17. Early-warning curve and its follow-ups (2026-10-30)

- **Question.** Can the habit be seen coming? [measured, RUNLOG l.765]
- **Design.** No training. Loop gain and offset at every saved checkpoint; a pre-registered held-out test on r9; a margin-to-rail test [measured, RUNLOG l.765, l.769, l.773].
- **Result (verified).**
  - The loop gain turns positive one checkpoint before the first over-bar episode in s42 and s60. But late s80 reaches the same loop state with no over-bar episode [measured, RUNLOG l.769].
  - The r9 held-out test FAILS: the only testable signal fired in all 5 r9 runs by 2.06M, including the cleanest negative (s70) [measured, RUNLOG l.773].
  - Late s80 was as close to the rail as s42 one checkpoint before its first over-bar, but approaching 4-12 times more slowly [measured, RUNLOG l.773].
- **Status.** Final. No validated warning [measured, RUNLOG l.769, l.773].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.765-773. Records PR #656.

### E18. BS: first critic-blind screen (2026-10-30)

- **Question.** Does hiding the tail_3 angle (observation 6) from the critic only stop the early rise? [measured, RUNLOG l.772]
- **Design.** 8 CPU continuations from stance6 s42, 1,048,576 to 2,490,368 (1.44M steps): 4 control, 4 critic-blind, seeds 2101-2131. Primary: the on-policy tail_3 command over the last 8 updates. Gate: the control median must rise at least 0.10. Exact permutation test. Run under the maintainer's overnight authorisation [measured, RUNLOG l.764, l.775-776].
- **Result line.** "line 1, NOT INFORMATIVE: the control arm did not reproduce the early rise (control median primary +0.0603, rise +0.0918 from B_S -0.0316, against the pre-registered 0.10); no reading about the critic is made." [measured, RUNLOG l.779]
- **Key numbers (report only).** Arm means +0.093 (control) and +0.013 (blind); p 13/70. Verified by two checks [measured, RUNLOG l.779-780].
- **Status.** Final: not informative [measured, RUNLOG l.779-780].
- **Record.** RUNLOG l.772-782. Durable `handoff-bias-screen` at cfed2c70 [measured, RUNLOG l.782]. Records PR #656, merged 2026-10-31 about 14:30 UTC [measured, RUNLOG l.814].

