  - Fetch (F2) from 16:39 UTC; 410 copies equal to the run manifests; all six runs COMPLETE [measured, RUNLOG l.960-967].
- **Pinned result line.** "READING: line 4: NO TAIL RAIL OR PARK IN 3 OF 3 PHASE-CRITIC RUNS, THE STANCE GATE CERTIFICATE PASSED IN 3 OF 3 (GATE CERTIFICATE: final checkpoint, measured on a screen task; not certification), NO SATURATING HABIT ON ANOTHER ACTUATOR: CONSISTENT WITH THE PHASE CRITIC REMOVING THE HABIT, NOT CONFIRMATORY (descriptive: 3 phase-critic runs beside 3 concurrent switch-off runs; KNOWN LIMITS)". STATUS: FINAL [measured, `ST/f2/score/score_pc.txt` lines 357, 365].
- **THE ONE TEST, pinned.** "NOT SEPARATED (p = 20/20)". The three OFF runs entered as missing because they were not blind [measured, `score_pc.txt` line 362]. This is a FAIL of the pre-registered test, caused by the procedural slip.
- **THE ONE TEST, flagged deviation reading.** "LOWER THAN EVERY CONCURRENT SWITCH-OFF RUN (exact permutation p = 1/20)" [measured, `ST/f2/score/score_pc_dev.txt` line 393]. Not the pinned reading: it was decided after the slip and assumes the slip had no effect on the OFF runs [measured, RUNLOG l.969].
- **Key numbers.**

| Seed | PHASE: tail class, gate, other habit | PHASE TD | OFF: tail class, gate, other habit | OFF TD |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| s60 | CLEAR, PASS, none | 0.0079 | PARKED (tail_3 MEAN_a +0.642), PASS, none | 0.388 |
| s42 | CLEAR, PASS, none | 0.0173 | RAIL (22 tail alarms from 3,932,160), FAIL, none | 0.635 |
| s80 | CLEAR, PASS, none | 0.0122 | CLEAR, PASS, neck_pitch SATURATING (6 alarms) | 0.154 |

  [measured, `score_pc.txt` lines 321-343, 362]
  - Per seed, OFF TD is 13 to 49 times PHASE TD (s80 12.6, s42 36.7, s60 49.1) [measured, computed from `score_pc.txt` line 362].
  - PHASE runs' highest evaluation tail command: 0.021, 0.030, 0.031 (s60, s42, s80). No evaluation reached 0.30 [measured, `score_pc.txt` lines 322, 326, 330].
  - Report only: PHASE mean returns 4442.7, 4481.0, 4482.3 against OFF 4412.6, 4377.7, 4415.8 [measured, `score_pc.txt` lines 324, 328, 332, 337, 341, 347].
  - Report only, a NEGATIVE: PHASE s60 had 9 falls in 910 evaluation episodes; every other run had 0 or 1 [measured, same lines].
  - If the phase input changed nothing, "no rail in 3 runs" would still have a 0.296 chance (plug-in at 1 of 3) [measured, `score_pc.txt` line 359].
